      "role": "user",
      "content": "but finding a way forward is the problem. there is no \"forward\" that isn't just me constantly looking over my shoulder waiting for the next thing to fall apart. i've always been the one who had it all together, the one they could actually rely on. if i can't even do that anymore, what's the point? it feels like my whole identity was just a lie. i feel like i've already failed them, and now i just have to live with being this broken version of myself forever. it feels so much easier to just stop trying than to face them every single day.",
